{"id": "EUVD-2026-102507", "enisaUuid": "d4863bf4-9704-37d6-b423-cd552260d7ee", "description": "BillionMail through 4.9 contains a hard-coded cryptographic key vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to forge unsubscribe and subscribe-confirm JWTs by computing the key from shipped configuration constants. Attackers can submit forged tokens to /api/unsubscribe, /api/unsubscribe_new, or /api/subscribe/confirm to deactivate any contact or force confirmed subscriptions.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T21:43:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T01:53:10", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/billionmail-unsubscribe-subscribe-jwt-deterministic-secret-forgery", "https://github.com/aaPanel/BillionMail/blob/v4.9/core/internal/service/batch_mail/jwt.go#L98-L123", "https://github.com/aaPanel/BillionMail/blob/v4.9/core/manifest/config/config.yaml", "https://github.com/aaPanel/BillionMail", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/billionmail-through-4.9-forgeable-jwts-via-default-signing-key"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111367", "GHSA-h86v-9fhw-gvch"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "749a3bbc-0ba3-35dc-a73c-ac70a847b12c", "product": {"name": "BillionMail", "vendor": {"name": "aapanel"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22644.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5b62a658-46a8-3e6e-aa57-5362a37e6e85", "vendor": {"name": "aapanel"}}], "isExploited": false}